WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.233 --> 00:00:00.567
Well, Mr.

00:00:00.567 --> 00:00:02.635
Trump is giving every indication

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:04.037
he intends to ignore

00:00:04.037 --> 00:00:05.238
the new special counsel,

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:07.741
calling him, quote, super radical left.

00:00:08.108 --> 00:00:09.743
And even though the investigations

00:00:09.743 --> 00:00:11.678
have been going on for months,

00:00:11.678 --> 00:00:12.045
the former

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:12.746
president acted

00:00:12.746 --> 00:00:14.614
surprised that they are still

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:16.049
very active.

00:00:16.049 --> 00:00:16.816
Here's what he told

00:00:16.816 --> 00:00:17.684
a crowd on Friday

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:20.620
night at his Florida resort

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:23.023
a weaponized Department of Justice.

00:00:23.023 --> 00:00:24.591
Would you like me to talk about that?

00:00:24.591 --> 00:00:27.560
Larry, would you like me to talk about

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.462
this horrendous abuse of power

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:30.196
is the latest

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:32.465
in a long series of witch hunts

00:00:33.433 --> 00:00:35.535
started a long time ago.

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:37.170
I thought the investigation

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:38.705
with the document hoax

00:00:38.705 --> 00:00:41.274
was dying or dead or over.

00:00:41.274 --> 00:00:44.244
And the investigation into January six

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:46.046
and my very peaceful

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:47.213
and patriotic speech

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:49.682
remember peaceful and patriotically

00:00:50.417 --> 00:00:52.719
was dead, especially after the record

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:53.686
setting 40 point

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:54.854
loss of Liz Cheney

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:56.322
in the great state of Wyoming.

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:57.624
I thought it was dead.

00:00:57.624 --> 00:00:58.191
I thought that

00:00:58.191 --> 00:01:00.326
put the final nail in the coffin,

00:01:01.161 --> 00:01:02.195
only to find out

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:03.063
that the corrupt

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:05.565
and highly political Justice Department

00:01:06.166 --> 00:01:09.102
just appointed a super radical left

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:10.770
special counsel,

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:11.471
better referred

00:01:11.471 --> 00:01:13.239
to as a special prosecutor,

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:15.208
to start the process all over again.

00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:16.743
We thought it was just about dead

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:20.080
Jessica Levinson is a

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:21.114
professor of law

00:01:21.114 --> 00:01:23.316
at Loyola Law School and joins me now

00:01:23.316 --> 00:01:24.084
from Los Angeles.

00:01:24.084 --> 00:01:25.819
She is also the host

00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:28.321
of The Passing Judgment Podcast.

00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:29.622
So good to see you.

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:31.424
How will this impact Mr.

00:01:31.424 --> 00:01:34.094
Trump's campaign to run for president?

00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:35.095
I actually don't know

00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:35.495
that it's

00:01:35.495 --> 00:01:36.329
going to impact

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:37.030
the campaign

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:37.630
that much

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:39.099
because we've already seen the former

00:01:39.099 --> 00:01:40.200
president say

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:40.600
all of

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:42.035
this is illegitimate,

00:01:42.035 --> 00:01:44.537
the investigations are illegitimate.

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:45.772
Any sort of indictment,

00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:46.206
he'll say,

00:01:46.206 --> 00:01:48.408
is also just a political witch hunt.

00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:49.776
So the decision

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:51.444
to appoint a special counsel,

00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:52.412
I think it's important

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:54.047
for the Department of Justice.

00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:55.081
It's important for people

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:56.549
who believe in the rule of law

00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:57.650
and the independence

00:01:57.650 --> 00:01:59.252
of the Department of Justice.

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:00.620
But for the former president

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:01.821
and his campaign, he's

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:03.790
just going to keep feeding people

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:06.092
the same diet of disinformation

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:08.328
and say there's no there there.

00:02:08.328 --> 00:02:10.830
But why bring in a special counsel

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:11.464
right now?

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:13.766
Why not allow the DOJ

00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:16.769
to move forward with its investigations?

00:02:17.971 --> 00:02:19.939
I think because two things have happened.

00:02:19.939 --> 00:02:21.841
One, the midterms are now over.

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:22.342
And two,

00:02:22.342 --> 00:02:22.742
the former

00:02:22.742 --> 00:02:23.676
president has said,

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:26.279
I am a candidate for the presidency.

00:02:26.279 --> 00:02:27.046
Again,

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:29.782
And so what we see here is potentially

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:31.351
another matchup

00:02:31.351 --> 00:02:32.752
between President Biden

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:34.721
and former President Trump.

00:02:34.721 --> 00:02:36.556
And we have an attorney general

00:02:36.556 --> 00:02:38.091
who was appointed by one of those

00:02:38.091 --> 00:02:39.092
two men, obviously,

00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:41.094
who was appointed by President Biden.

00:02:41.094 --> 00:02:41.494
So, well,

00:02:41.494 --> 00:02:44.230
the Department of Justice is independent.

00:02:44.531 --> 00:02:45.131
What I think

00:02:45.131 --> 00:02:47.200
Merrick Garland recognized today

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:48.101
is that

00:02:48.101 --> 00:02:49.035
he doesn't want it

00:02:49.035 --> 00:02:51.371
to look like a political appointee

00:02:51.571 --> 00:02:53.373
of one of the candidates.

00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:54.240
President Biden

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:55.675
is just trying to take down

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:57.043
the other candidate,

00:02:57.043 --> 00:02:58.745
former President Trump.

00:02:58.745 --> 00:02:59.479
The other thing

00:02:59.479 --> 00:03:01.681
is this actually insulates

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:03.116
Attorney General Merrick Garland

00:03:03.116 --> 00:03:04.651
a little bit, because now that House

00:03:04.651 --> 00:03:06.452
Republicans will be in control,

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:07.954
they're going to have a lot of hearings

00:03:07.954 --> 00:03:09.789
about these investigations.

00:03:09.789 --> 00:03:11.257
And if he has a special counsel,

00:03:11.257 --> 00:03:12.091
he can say, you know what,

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:12.959
I'm not involved

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:14.627
in these investigations anymore.

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:16.329
I can't answer your questions.

00:03:16.329 --> 00:03:17.597
So I think there are really

00:03:17.597 --> 00:03:18.865
a number of reasons

00:03:18.865 --> 00:03:21.134
why this is the timing that he chose.

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:23.036
Now, talk to us a little bit

00:03:23.036 --> 00:03:24.170
about the counsel.

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:25.338
Who is the counsel

00:03:25.338 --> 00:03:26.906
what can you tell us about Mr.

00:03:26.906 --> 00:03:27.707
Jack Smith?

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:30.910
So he is a former federal prosecutor.

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:31.844
And I think at this point,

00:03:31.844 --> 00:03:33.346
people are so used to hearing

00:03:33.346 --> 00:03:34.681
former federal prosecutor,

00:03:34.681 --> 00:03:35.515
that means he worked

00:03:35.515 --> 00:03:37.150
in the Department of Justice.

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:38.551
And it would be very surprising

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:39.085
to have somebody

00:03:39.085 --> 00:03:41.254
without that baseline experience.

00:03:41.254 --> 00:03:44.490
But we also know that he has experience

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:46.059
in the public in Hegarty

00:03:46.059 --> 00:03:46.793
unit dealing

00:03:46.793 --> 00:03:48.294
with public corruption crimes.

00:03:48.294 --> 00:03:50.063
I think that's really significant.

00:03:50.063 --> 00:03:51.364
The other significant thing here

00:03:51.364 --> 00:03:52.298
is that he's actually been

00:03:52.298 --> 00:03:53.199
abroad, working

00:03:53.199 --> 00:03:55.201
the International Criminal Court

00:03:55.201 --> 00:03:55.868
dealing with things

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:57.103
like war crimes,

00:03:57.103 --> 00:03:59.872
also corruption and investigations

00:03:59.872 --> 00:04:00.473
and charges

00:04:00.473 --> 00:04:02.242
against former government

00:04:02.242 --> 00:04:03.943
officials of foreign states.

00:04:03.943 --> 00:04:06.045
That's about as close to the experience

00:04:06.045 --> 00:04:08.114
of investigating a former president

00:04:08.114 --> 00:04:09.649
as you can possibly get.

00:04:09.649 --> 00:04:11.484
So you think for those reasons,

00:04:11.484 --> 00:04:12.785
this particular decision

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:14.687
makes a lot of sense

00:04:14.687 --> 00:04:16.756
And what investigations

00:04:16.756 --> 00:04:17.991
is this special counsel

00:04:17.991 --> 00:04:19.959
going to be overseeing?

00:04:19.959 --> 00:04:21.794
Yeah, great. Great question.

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:22.695
The special counsel

00:04:22.695 --> 00:04:23.663
is going to be looking

00:04:23.663 --> 00:04:24.297
at the

00:04:24.297 --> 00:04:25.598
two investigations

00:04:25.598 --> 00:04:27.100
involving the former president

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:28.368
on the federal level.

00:04:28.368 --> 00:04:31.404
And so the first investigation involves

00:04:31.404 --> 00:04:33.773
the activities around January

00:04:33.773 --> 00:04:36.209
six, 20, 21, and specifically

00:04:36.409 --> 00:04:37.310
whether or not the former

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:38.611
president could be guilty

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:40.079
of something like defrauding

00:04:40.079 --> 00:04:41.347
the United States

00:04:41.347 --> 00:04:43.216
by trying to thwart the peaceful

00:04:43.216 --> 00:04:44.484
transfer of power

00:04:44.484 --> 00:04:47.020
and stopping Congress from doing its duty

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:47.520
that day,

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:48.521
which was certifying

00:04:48.521 --> 00:04:50.156
Electoral College votes.

00:04:50.156 --> 00:04:51.457
The other thing they're looking at

00:04:51.457 --> 00:04:53.626
is the Mar a Lago investigation

00:04:53.626 --> 00:04:55.128
related to the former president

00:04:55.128 --> 00:04:57.830
apparently illegally retaining documents

00:04:57.830 --> 00:04:58.931
that were classified

00:04:58.931 --> 00:05:00.533
and highly sensitive.

00:05:00.533 --> 00:05:02.602
These are very different investigations.

00:05:02.602 --> 00:05:04.103
But the special counsel will be

00:05:04.103 --> 00:05:05.371
overseeing both of them.

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:07.440
And talk to us a little

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:09.309
bit about the time frame.

00:05:09.309 --> 00:05:11.711
What's the timeline for this?

00:05:11.711 --> 00:05:14.414
So we don't know a specific timeline,

00:05:14.414 --> 00:05:17.717
and that's entirely normal.

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:19.652
We would never know a timeline

00:05:19.652 --> 00:05:21.788
until there are filings in court.

00:05:22.021 --> 00:05:23.690
And that leaves us some breadcrumbs

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:25.491
about figuring out

00:05:25.491 --> 00:05:26.793
how close are they to

00:05:26.793 --> 00:05:28.561
a potential indictment.

00:05:28.561 --> 00:05:29.729
One thing to note

00:05:29.729 --> 00:05:30.596
is that

00:05:30.596 --> 00:05:31.864
in terms of the timeline,

00:05:31.864 --> 00:05:34.600
to kind of zoom out for a little bit,

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:36.069
the fact that a special counsel

00:05:36.069 --> 00:05:37.136
was appointed at all

00:05:37.136 --> 00:05:39.072
for both of these investigations

00:05:39.072 --> 00:05:40.073
indicates

00:05:40.073 --> 00:05:42.842
that they are very much live and ongoing

00:05:42.842 --> 00:05:45.144
and could potentially lead to indictments

00:05:45.144 --> 00:05:47.213
if both of these investigations

00:05:47.213 --> 00:05:47.947
were winding

00:05:47.947 --> 00:05:49.882
down were in their end stages.

00:05:49.882 --> 00:05:51.217
There really is no point

00:05:51.217 --> 00:05:52.952
for taking this historic step

00:05:52.952 --> 00:05:54.787
and appointing a special counsel.

00:05:54.787 --> 00:05:56.489
But I think it indicates

00:05:56.489 --> 00:05:57.724
not exactly where we are

00:05:57.724 --> 00:05:58.658
in the timeline,

00:05:58.658 --> 00:06:01.994
but these are very real investigations

00:06:01.994 --> 00:06:03.563
and that there is a they're there

00:06:03.563 --> 00:06:04.964
maybe not an indictment,

00:06:04.964 --> 00:06:06.265
but there is certainly something

00:06:06.265 --> 00:06:07.233
they're looking at in

00:06:07.233 --> 00:06:08.668
both of these cases.

